# Test: ze root namespace grammar — traffic/isis/ospf splits, update serve, removed names
# VALIDATES: `ze traffic control`, `ze isis decode`, `ze ospf decode`, `ze update serve`
#            route to their tools; bare `ze traffic|isis|ospf` are discoverable (AC-10);
#            the five old hyphenated/mis-named roots are gone (AC-9).
# // STRENGTHENING. Per-command exit is now the inline `cmd=...:exit=N`
# form (standalone `expect=exit:code` is FILE-level/last-wins and was dead for every
# step but the last), and every `contains` needle is now UNIQUE to its command
# ("usage: ze traffic <command>", "unknown command: <old-name>") so the runner's
# cumulative combined-output match cannot satisfy a step vacuously from another step.
# Discoverability of the member list is additionally proven by the Go unit tests
# TestTrafficSubDispatch / TestISISSubDispatch / TestOSPFSubDispatch. Real decode/serve
# behavior: test/isis-wire/, test/ospf-wire/, test/ui/update-serve.ci.

# traffic control routes to the tc/VPP tool (usage line is unique to `traffic control`)
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze traffic control --help:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=ze traffic control <command>

# bare `ze traffic` enumerates its members (AC-10); the "usage: ze traffic <command>"
# line is emitted ONLY by the bare-root dispatcher, not by `traffic control`.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze traffic:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=usage: ze traffic <command>

# isis decode routes to the offline codec
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze isis decode --help:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=usage: ze isis decode

# bare `ze isis` enumerates its members (AC-10)
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze isis:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=usage: ze isis <command>

# ospf decode routes to the offline codec
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=ze ospf decode --help:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=usage: ze ospf decode

# bare `ze ospf` enumerates its members (AC-10)
cmd=foreground:seq=6:exec=ze ospf:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=usage: ze ospf <command>

# `ze update serve` routes through the update YANG verb to runUpdateServe with
# --listen intact: an unbindable port makes the real listener fail fast, and the
# port value echoed in the output proves the flag propagated (AC-8 routing half;
# the successful-listen half is test/ui/update-serve.ci).
cmd=foreground:seq=7:exec=ze update serve --listen 127.0.0.1:65600:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=65600

# The five old names are gone, not aliased (AC-9) — each needle names the exact
# old command so no step can satisfy another's assertion.
cmd=foreground:seq=8:exec=ze traffic-control:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=unknown command: traffic-control

cmd=foreground:seq=9:exec=ze isis-decode:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=unknown command: isis-decode

cmd=foreground:seq=10:exec=ze ospf-decode:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=unknown command: ospf-decode

cmd=foreground:seq=11:exec=ze update-serve:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=unknown command: update-serve
